        </div>
        <p>
            In absence of friction, the direction of the contact force is perpendicular to the surface of contact. <strong>Friction</strong> is also due to electromagnetic force and it's direction is parallel to the contact surface. 
        </p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h2>Tension</h2>
        <p>Some times two objects are connected via a string. When a string is pulled, there is <em>tension</em> in the string. The source of this force is electromagnetic force. The direction of this force is along the string.</p>
