    <section>
        <h2>Force due to a Spring</h2>
        <p>
            Springs play import role in mechanical systems. When a spring is stretched or compressed it exerts <em>spring force</em> on the attached object. The origin of this force is electromagnetism as well. A spring has a natural length (say {`\\(L\\)`}) when it is neither stretched nor compressed. At this length, there is no spring force. When the spring is compressed or stretched by an amount {`\\(x\\)`}, the spring force is given by {`\\[F=-kx\\]`} where minus sign shows that the spring resists stretching or compressing.
        </p>
        <br>
